  "quality_flags": [
    {
      "flag_type": "unresolved_inconsistency",
      "slot": "preconditions",
      "detail": "[trigger_preconditions_coverage] The main flow requires the Operator to request command control from a specified workstation, but Preconditions does not assert that the Operator is at an authorized/specified workstation before initiating the request. (atomic grounding: candidate remains incomplete (Evidence does not establish that the Operator is at the workstation, that the workstation is authorized for command control acquisition, or that acquisition is an explicit condition.))",
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "flag_type": "unresolved_inconsistency",
      "slot": "exception_flow",
      "detail": "[exceptionflow_exit_coverage] The exception flow branch only states that the system asks the Operator to accept or deny command control; it does not document any outcome after acceptance or denial, so the branch lacks a clear return, termination/handoff, or terminal failure/prevention state. (still no supporting evidence after retrieval)",
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "flag_type": "unresolved_inconsistency",
      "slot": "exception_flow",
      "detail": "[exceptionflow_exit_coverage] The exception flow branch stops at the system requesting the Operator to accept or deny command control. It does not state what happens after acceptance or denial, and provides no return to main flow, termination/handoff, or explicit terminal failure/prevention state for this branch. (still no supporting evidence after retrieval)",
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "flag_type": "unresolved_inconsistency",
      "slot": "preconditions",
      "detail": "[mainflow_postconditions_reachability] Precondition claim 3 states the Operator is the only Operator logged on, but main flow step 4 and postcondition 4 require handling another user who previously had command control and must be notified. This precondition makes that takeover/notification postcondition unreachable under the stated starting conditions.",
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "flag_type": "unresolved_inconsistency",
      "slot": "exception_flow",
      "detail": "[exceptionflow_exit_coverage] The exception flow's only claim ends with the system requesting the Operator to accept or deny command control. It does not specify the outcome after acceptance or denial, so neither branch has a clear exit: return to main flow, terminate/hand off, or an explicit failure/prevention state.",
      "evidence_refs": []
    }
  ],
